WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.459
Want to visit Barbie land?

00:00:01.459 --> 00:00:03.050
Because I figured out where it is.

00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:04.860
No roller blading required.

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:06.160
Though, fair warning.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:11.430
You might want to bring your passport.

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:12.680
Hello Internet!

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:14.559
Welcome to Film Theory.

00:00:14.559 --> 00:00:15.559
The show that accepts

00:00:15.559 --> 00:00:19.760
that in a world full of Barbies and Kens,
sometimes it's best to just be an Alan.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.779
Man, the Internet was hyped for the Barbie
movie, weren't they?

00:00:22.779 --> 00:00:26.130
I swear, you couldn't scroll
for more than 2 seconds on Twitter...

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:27.240
X... threads?

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:28.900
I don't know.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:30.609
You couldn't scroll for more than 2

00:00:30.609 --> 00:00:34.140
seconds on insert generic social media
feed here without being bombarded

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:38.560
by someone unleashing their inner Kenergy
or rockin’ their newest hot pink outfit.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:41.789
So of course, I had to see
if all the hype was warranted.

00:00:41.789 --> 00:00:45.450
And as I walked out of the theater,
I realized, yeah, I kind of loved it.

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:49.320
Sure, the theme was a bit on the nose for
my taste, but man, the movie was just fun

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:51.590
across the board,
an awesome cast of characters

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:54.640
that are just dropped into the middle
of one of the coolest and most interesting

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:57.090
fictional worlds
that I've seen in a long time.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:00.239
A world that I and many others
would probably want to visit

00:01:00.239 --> 00:01:01.820
if only it were real.

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:02.949
Except it is real.

00:01:02.949 --> 00:01:03.949
Now,

00:01:03.949 --> 00:01:05.519
right off the bat,
I might have lost you on that one.

00:01:05.519 --> 00:01:07.930
Barbie Land is clearly meant
to be a fictional location, right?

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:09.240
They even explicitly distinguish

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:11.920
between the real world in the movie
and Barbie Land.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:15.450
So aren't they clearly trying to tell us
that Barbie Land is a fake world?

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:17.340
Well,
that's what I thought initially, too.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:21.000
But everything else that we see in the
film gives more evidence to the contrary.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.420
When Margot Robbie's
Barbie meets with Kate McKinnon's

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:26.840
Weird Barbie to discuss the odd things
that have been happening in the world,

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:29.860
Weird Barbie describes
the passageway between the real world

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:31.690
and Barbie Land as a portal.

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:34.920
Considering the fact that portals don't,
you know, tend to exist here on Earth,

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:35.920
that would seem to tell us that

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:39.020
Barbie Land is in some separate dimension
from the real world.

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:41.960
However, this is immediately
contradicted a few moments later

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:45.159
when Weird Barbie admits
that the portal was just a metaphor.

00:01:45.159 --> 00:01:48.259
She then whips out her trusty
instruction manual, courtesy of Mattel,

00:01:48.259 --> 00:01:51.391
to tell Barbie the step by step directions
for how to get from Barbie Land

00:01:51.391 --> 00:01:54.329
to the real world,
specifically Los Angeles.

00:01:54.329 --> 00:01:55.540
I've been to Los Angeles.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:59.061
I wouldn't exactly call it the real world,
but then again, who am I to judge?

00:01:59.061 --> 00:02:00.270
To get from Barbie Land to L.A.

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:03.590
the instructions tell us that Barbie
needs to take a sports car, a speedboat,

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:07.189
a rocket ship, a tandem bicycle,
a camper van, a snowmobile.

00:02:07.189 --> 00:02:10.770
And then finally don a pair of roller
skates to blade all the way to Santa

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:11.770
Monica Beach.

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:12.770
Now, these aren't

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:16.070
so much Google map directions as they are
just a list of modes of transportation.

00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:18.160
It’d be like me
telling you how to get to my house

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:20.269
by saying you have to take a plane,
a bus and a car.

00:02:20.269 --> 00:02:22.360
You're missing a few key details there.

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:23.360
We can also rule out

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:26.730
that these comically pink propulsion
devices are meant to be magical.

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:29.950
Both Kens and Barbies
as well as real human for able to travel

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:33.220
freely back and forth between Barbie Land
and the real world, provided

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:35.760
they follow these instructions
either forward or backward.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:37.490
So while the idea of trying
to find the real world

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:40.610
Barbie Land might seem dumb at first,
it is possible

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:43.879
according to the canon of the movie,
and that's the kind of fine line

00:02:43.879 --> 00:02:45.810
that we love to ride on this channel.

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:48.040
So instead of finishing my Barbenheimer
double feature,

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:51.300
I bid my family adieu and rushed
home, unfurled the world map

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:54.879
and tried to pinpoint
exactly where Mattel is hiding Barbie Land.

00:02:54.879 --> 00:02:55.879
And let me tell you.

00:02:55.879 --> 00:02:56.879
Despite the movie

00:02:56.879 --> 00:02:59.400
seemingly going out of its way to dissuade
theorists like us from doing exactly

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.870
that, they gave us
just the perfect amount of breadcrumbs

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:04.830
that led us right to the doorstep
of that pink paradise.

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:06.980
Oh ho, I figured you out, Mattel.

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:08.760
You’re going to have to try a lot harder
than that

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:09.920
to keep your boy MatPat

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:13.700
from going to live out his dream
of being a Barbie girl in a Barbie world.

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:16.760
So grab your pink
stilettos, Birkenstocks and Google Maps

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:20.680
dear theorists, as I once
and for all chart a course to Barbie Land.

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:24.050
Let's start by throwing out some possible
locations that Barbie Land can't be.

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:28.110
In the movie, one of the characters asks
if Barbie Land is in an alternate reality.

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:30.810
Basically asking the movie the exact
question that I desperately needed.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.459
The CEO of Mattel, played by Will

00:03:32.459 --> 00:03:36.010
Ferrell, says that “you can think of it
as a small town in Sweden”.

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:38.510
Now it's clear that in this moment
he's trying to change the subject.

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:39.510
After all, his main

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:40.939
aim in
the movie is to make sure that Barbie Land

00:03:40.939 --> 00:03:43.349
and the real world
stay as isolated as possible.

00:03:43.349 --> 00:03:46.080
That said, could Barbie Land
actually be in Sweden?

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:47.080
No.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:48.810
Several times throughout the movie,
we see characters taking a sports

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:52.209
car just outside of Barbie Land,
only to find themselves in a desert.

00:03:52.209 --> 00:03:53.670
Sweden is many things.

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:55.190
A desert,
it is not.

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:57.090
This information
also allows us to rule out

00:03:57.090 --> 00:04:00.360
my sneaky early pick for Barbie Land,
which was Wisconsin.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:02.420
As it turns out, Barbie, the toy’s

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:06.239
canonical Hometown, is the fictional city
of Willows, Wisconsin.

00:04:06.239 --> 00:04:09.150
Since this movie did such a good job
of making deep cut references to past

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:10.540
Barbie lore,
it would have been fitting to see

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:13.770
Barbie Land's real location
paying homage to her lesser known home.

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:17.799
But alas, Wisconsin is the antithesis
of a desert, so our search must continue.

00:04:17.799 --> 00:04:21.820
Now, as much fun as it’d be to rule out
every single location on Earth one by one,

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:24.440
there has to be a more straightforward
approach to solving the mystery.

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:27.550
Eventually, I realized that instead of
just trying to eliminate where Barbie Land

00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:30.490
couldn't be, we had to follow the route
laid out by the movie.

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:32.400
We needed to use
each mode of transportation

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:34.560
and then cross-referenc locations
on the map to see

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:38.270
if we could create a travel itinerary
that would actually find Barbie's Malibu

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:39.270
dream house.

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:41.000
And not to bury the lead here.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:43.200
But it's not as easy
as just being in Malibu.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.690
Since we obviously don't know
our starting location,

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:46.750
the only thing we can really do

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:50.280
is go through our pre-established journey
in reverse, starting in Los Angeles,

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:52.430
and then working backwards
through the modes of transportation

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:55.030
until we eventually stumble
our way back into Barbie Land.

00:04:55.030 --> 00:04:56.190
The first leg we need to look into

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:59.830
is crossing into California
while wearing neon and roller skates.

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:01.750
The way it's phrased in
the movie is a little bit odd.

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:03.900
It goes like this, quote,
The snowmobile will take you

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:07.100
most of the way to the state of Los
Angeles, where you will don

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:10.479
Neon and rollerblades
and enter the country of California.

00:05:10.479 --> 00:05:12.910
Now, clearly,
there are some mistakes there.

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:15.800
A recurring joke throughout the movie
is that the Barbies are overall ignorant

00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:17.000
to real world things.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.400
So weird Barbie getting confused

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:21.699
about the difference between states
and countries is no big surprise.

00:05:21.699 --> 00:05:24.250
It's also worth noting
that while Weird Barbie is saying this,

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:27.200
she's clearly pointing to the Los Angeles
area on the map.

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:28.490
So you could argue that she doesn't

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:31.980
really mean crossing into the border
of the state of California at all.

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:34.669
Regardless, I tried to solve this one
in two different ways.

00:05:34.669 --> 00:05:36.900
The first was taking what she said
literally,

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:39.800
and looking at the closest places
where Barbie could cross into the state

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:43.160
of California
after having just got off of a snowmobile.

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:46.490
The three states that immediately
surround California are Oregon, Nevada

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:47.490
and Arizona.

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:50.060
Taking an aerial view
of those three potential entry points.

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:52.449
One of these things is clearly
not like the others.

00:05:52.449 --> 00:05:54.850
While
Arizona and Nevada are clearly scorching

00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:57.900
deserts, Oregon, it's a much better fit
for our snowmobile stop.

00:05:57.900 --> 00:06:01.080
It has plenty of snow capped mountains
and a thriving snowmobile industry.

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:03.430
It also, conveniently
enough, had not just one

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:07.330
but two snowmobile rental spots
just across the Oregon-California border

00:06:07.330 --> 00:06:08.650
in the town of Medford.

00:06:08.650 --> 00:06:12.090
So we drop off our snowmobiles in Medford,
lace up our roller skates

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:15.080
and head on down the California coastline
until we get to sunny Los

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:19.099
Angeles, is what I'd be saying
if it wasn't such a long trip.

00:06:19.099 --> 00:06:21.920
See if we're crossing the border
all the way up at the north.

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:22.920
We are now forced

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:27.050
to skate the entire length of California,
and that is a long trip.

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:30.310
That is taking 11
plus days to get down to Los Angeles.

00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:32.430
I mean, Barbie's not one to skip leg day

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:35.751
and if we want to take Weird Barbie
at her word, it's our most probable bet.

00:06:35.751 --> 00:06:37.310
But is it our best bet?

00:06:37.310 --> 00:06:38.470
So I took another look.

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:41.410
If we wanted somewhere
that was a bit closer, Lake Tahoe area

00:06:41.410 --> 00:06:44.740
tucked right here away in the Sierra
Nevada mountains is a slightly closer

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:48.180
possibility for this penultimate leg
of the journey, but not by a whole lot.

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:51.270
You see, starting from here,
Ken and Barbie are spending about six days

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:53.360
in roller skates
trying to get down to Hollywood.

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:54.360
Better.

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:55.490
But still in the realm of ridiculous.

00:06:55.490 --> 00:06:56.490
I don't know.

00:06:56.490 --> 00:06:59.680
To me, both of these routes just felt
too far fetched, which made me think

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:02.610
that weird Barbie was just off in her map
reading skills.

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:06.250
I mean, the maps in the movie leave a lot
to be desired in terms of accuracy.

00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:07.250
Like here, we see that

00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:10.970
New York is practically up in Canada
and England is down near the equator,

00:07:10.970 --> 00:07:15.800
making London a tropical paradise rather
than the cool foggy town it normally is.

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:19.349
And again, in her directions, weird Barbie
already flip flopped state and country,

00:07:19.349 --> 00:07:21.630
so I decided to tackle this a second way.

00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:24.190
Maybe what she was meaning to say
is that after snowmobiling,

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:28.440
you cross into the county of Los Angeles,
in the state of California,

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:32.030
which then gives us a lot more realistic
possibilities.

00:07:32.030 --> 00:07:35.190
Specifically here, the San Gabriel
and San Bernardino Mountains,

00:07:35.190 --> 00:07:38.160
literally an hour's
drive outside of Los Angeles.

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:39.160
Here we have ourselves beautiful

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:42.310
snow capped mountains, perfect
for snowmobiling, and better yet, perfect

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:46.460
for rollerblading into the city
at a mere 12 to 14 hour journey.

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:48.580
It's certainly long,
but it is far more attainable

00:07:48.580 --> 00:07:52.310
than the multi-day or even multi-week
trips of our other options.

00:07:52.310 --> 00:07:55.090
So I'm going to move forward
using that as my waypoint.

00:07:55.090 --> 00:07:56.090
What's next on the journey?

00:07:56.090 --> 00:07:57.870
Prior
to heading to Cali-for-nyw-ah.

00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:00.819
Ken and Barbie take a tandem bike,
followed by a camper van.

00:08:00.819 --> 00:08:02.460
While that sounds like a backpacker's
dream.

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:05.010
We're back to the same situation
we were in with the rollerblades.

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:08.120
You can basically take a bike and a van
just about anywhere you want to.

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:09.710
Leading to infinite possibilities.

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:12.030
Luckily,
we get ourselves some visual detail

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:14.419
that actually paint for us
a much clearer path.

00:08:14.419 --> 00:08:16.690
In the movie,
we get a montage of Barbie and Ken riding

00:08:16.690 --> 00:08:18.740
as they go through
each leg of their adventure.

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:20.849
In the tandem bike section,
we see them riding through

00:08:20.849 --> 00:08:22.270
a field of tulips and windmills.

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:25.220
Now when I see tulips and windmills,
the first place my mind goes to

00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:27.050
is the Netherlands or Denmark.

00:08:27.050 --> 00:08:30.509
But if I thought rollerblading down
an entire state seemed ridiculous,

00:08:30.509 --> 00:08:31.580
biking across the Atlantic?

00:08:31.580 --> 00:08:32.580
Yeah.

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:35.560
I tend to make some dumb theories,
but that one is just a bridge too far.

00:08:35.560 --> 00:08:38.460
Then I realized, well, sure,
it looks Dutch or Danish

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:39.909
that could just be an aesthetic choice.

00:08:39.909 --> 00:08:43.080
There must be places that are much closer
that look like it came straight

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:44.600
out of a postcard from Europe.

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:45.640
And sure enough, there are.

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:47.779
Doing a quick Google search
you see that Holland,

00:08:47.779 --> 00:08:51.300
Michigan is riffing off its namesake;
tulips and windmills for days.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:53.620
But still,
that's all the way across the country.

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:55.420
There has to be something
a bit more realistic,

00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:58.680
something a bit closer to the destinations
that we've already mapped out.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:00.130
And indeed, there is.

00:09:00.130 --> 00:09:03.690
Ladies and gentlemen, meet Solvang,
California, a small town located

00:09:03.690 --> 00:09:07.100
just outside of Los Angeles
that's decked out to look exactly like

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:11.310
a Danish town, complete with the tulips
and windmills and apple skiver.

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:14.520
Solvang looks exactly like the tandem
bike ride that we see in the movie.

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:18.339
And it's a mere 13 hour bike ride
just outside the city limits.

00:09:18.339 --> 00:09:19.339
Hmmm.

00:09:19.339 --> 00:09:20.709
Looks like we're starting
to see a pattern here.

00:09:20.709 --> 00:09:21.709
Fun side note, by the way,

00:09:21.709 --> 00:09:24.420
Solvang is where our head of production,
Jason, actually got engaged.

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:26.710
Good to know that Jason's
marriage is unironically helping me

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:29.150
to solve an insane theory
about the geography of the Barbie

00:09:29.150 --> 00:09:30.790
universe years later.

00:09:30.790 --> 00:09:31.790
#BlameJason?

00:09:31.790 --> 00:09:32.790
More like #ThanksJason.

00:09:32.790 --> 00:09:35.029
Also, on your way
there make sure you check out the pea soup

00:09:35.029 --> 00:09:36.300
at the nearby restaurants.

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:37.300
That seems random.

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:38.300
And it definitely is.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:39.649
But it's just what the highway restaurants

00:09:39.649 --> 00:09:41.690
advertise over in that area
and it's pretty good.

00:09:41.690 --> 00:09:44.610
Anyway, after a gentle tandem bike ride
through our discount Copenhagen,

00:09:44.610 --> 00:09:47.100
our plastic pals can rent a camper van
and make their way

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:49.020
to the San Gabriel Mountains,
where they’ll

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:52.620
then snowmobile around Mount Baldy
before rollerblading down to Hollywood.

00:09:52.620 --> 00:09:55.750
So far, so good and all nicely
contained within this nice little pocket

00:09:55.750 --> 00:09:56.930
of Southern California.

00:09:56.930 --> 00:10:00.230
Which brings us to the absolute
dumbest leg of the trip, the rocket ship.

00:10:00.230 --> 00:10:02.130
In the montage of Barbie
and Ken's journey,

00:10:02.130 --> 00:10:05.050
we see that
they ride a literal rocket into space.

00:10:05.050 --> 00:10:06.529
At first,
this made me think that Barbie Land

00:10:06.529 --> 00:10:08.720
was an interplanetary destination.

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:10.220
But now I'm not quite so sure.

00:10:10.220 --> 00:10:12.130
While having Barbie
be canonically an alien

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:15.589
would be hilarious and very on brand
for where we are in 2023,

00:10:15.589 --> 00:10:18.579
the step before this is riding a speedboat
and you wouldn't

00:10:18.579 --> 00:10:21.839
exactly be able to find any place
to run a speedboat over on Mars.

00:10:21.839 --> 00:10:24.120
So I think we're still dealing
with Earth here.

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:27.140
In fact, in that same scene,
we also see a brief glimpse of the Earth

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:29.350
and a suspicious looking pink shape
that kind of

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:30.950
looks like the outline of Barbie Land.

00:10:30.950 --> 00:10:32.760
If that's true,
then that means that the rocket ship

00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:34.540
is a bit of a fun detour for Barbie

00:10:34.540 --> 00:10:38.450
and Ken, allowing them to launch from
and then return back to the same spot.

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:40.220
That being said,
we still need to find the place that this

00:10:40.220 --> 00:10:44.089
would happen, preferably in tandem
biking distance from Solvang, California.

00:10:44.089 --> 00:10:46.100
So where could you possibly find
a rocket ship...

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:47.220
Oh, will you look at that?

00:10:47.220 --> 00:10:51.589
Located just 26 miles outside of Solvang
is none other than the Vandenberg Space

00:10:51.589 --> 00:10:53.920
Force base,
which features rocket launch pads

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:56.570
that are being used by both
NASA and Space X.

00:10:56.570 --> 00:10:58.100
What are the odds that a space

00:10:58.100 --> 00:11:01.060
port, of all things, would be so close
to our knock off Denmark?

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:03.240
It's almost like the writers planned it
this way.

00:11:03.240 --> 00:11:06.389
The launch pads also happen to be just
a stone's throw away from dozens of bike

00:11:06.389 --> 00:11:10.410
shops that allow for a tandem getaway
to the, quote, Danish capital of America.

00:11:10.410 --> 00:11:12.360
No, I'm not making any of this up.

00:11:12.360 --> 00:11:14.970
This is how cleanly all of this stuff
maps onto itself.

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:15.970
The Space Force base

00:11:15.970 --> 00:11:19.750
also butts up against the Pacific Ocean,
the perfect landing spot for a speedboat.

00:11:19.750 --> 00:11:23.149
Putting it all together, it's hard to deny
it feels like we're on the right track.

00:11:23.149 --> 00:11:25.940
We've made it
almost the entire way back to Barbie Land.

00:11:25.940 --> 00:11:29.020
We are so close
I can practically smell the plastic.

00:11:29.020 --> 00:11:31.110
So from Vandenberg,
we need to find a boat route

00:11:31.110 --> 00:11:32.810
that grants us access to a desert that can

00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:35.320
then be crossed via the Barbie sports car.

00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:36.340
Then and only then, will

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:39.760
we finally be able to locate
the mythical city decked out in pink.

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:43.149
Ladies and gentlemen, toys and girls,
I think I found the route.

00:11:43.149 --> 00:11:47.380
Barbie Land is located in none
other than, drum roll please.

00:11:47.380 --> 00:11:49.440
Monterrey, Mexico.

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:50.480
Yeah.

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:53.510
Barbie and the gang are living
la vida rosa down in Mexico.

00:11:53.510 --> 00:11:55.870
Monterrey,
located in the northeastern state of Nuevo

00:11:55.870 --> 00:11:59.740
Leon, is a beautiful city, flanked on
its western side by what, dear theorists?

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:01.170
The massive Chihuahuan Desert.

00:12:01.170 --> 00:12:02.769
By crossing the desert by car,

00:12:02.769 --> 00:12:05.769
you'd reach the Gulf of California
in about 8 to 10 hours.

00:12:05.769 --> 00:12:07.670
From there, you can board a speedboat
and ride your way

00:12:07.670 --> 00:12:09.270
all the way up the coast to Vandenberg's

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:12.920
Space Force base, then catch a quick ride
on one of Elon Musk's rockets,

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:15.800
go into low earth orbit and back
before renting a tandem bike to

00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:18.350
right all the way to Solvang,
catching a view of the tulips.

00:12:18.350 --> 00:12:21.520
After that, run a camper van
and ride up to the San Gabriel Mountains

00:12:21.520 --> 00:12:24.079
where you'll ditch your van for some cool
snowmobiles.

00:12:24.079 --> 00:12:25.930
Ride around
until lacing up some rollerblades

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:27.990
and taking the scenic route
through California

00:12:27.990 --> 00:12:31.230
to finally reach the, quote,
unquote, “real world” of Los Angeles.

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:34.360
Now, why would I choose Monterrey
specifically?

00:12:34.360 --> 00:12:36.220
Admittedly, when you look at the complete
map of the journey,

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:38.970
there are definitely some places
that are closer to Southern California

00:12:38.970 --> 00:12:41.950
that can still fit the bill of deserts
built up against an ocean.

00:12:41.950 --> 00:12:44.760
But consider this,
what else is located in Monterey, Mexico

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:48.560
but none other than the world's largest
Mattel factory.

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:53.550
With over 200,000 square meters of space
and over 3,500 employees.

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:55.230
Monterey is the perfect home
for Barbie in the movie

00:12:55.230 --> 00:12:59.010
because it quite literally
is the home for Barbie in the real world.

00:12:59.010 --> 00:13:02.710
Literally, Barbie Land; the land that makes
all the Barbies and houses all the Kens

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:04.519
and Alans and Skippers of the world.

00:13:04.519 --> 00:13:06.820
But as one final point of evidence
to seal the deal,

00:13:06.820 --> 00:13:10.020
in the movie when Ken starts to go
hyper masculine in his Kenergy,

00:13:10.020 --> 00:13:14.600
we do see some Kens actively building
a border wall outside of Barbie Land.

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:17.040
Now, I recognize that right
there's a political landmine.

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:18.170
But don't blame the messenger.

00:13:18.170 --> 00:13:19.220
I'm not the one who's doing it.

00:13:19.220 --> 00:13:20.370
I'm just saying it's in the movie.

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:21.750
And the subtext is obvious.

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:24.279
An army of Ken dolls
building a border wall?

00:13:24.279 --> 00:13:25.279
Yeah.

00:13:25.279 --> 00:13:26.279
It's just further evidence to prove

00:13:26.279 --> 00:13:29.830
that Barbie Land is at or near
the US-Mexico border.

00:13:29.830 --> 00:13:32.730
Exactly where Monterey
and its Mattel factory is.

00:13:32.730 --> 00:13:34.160
Where then is Barbie Land?

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:35.780
It's not as crazy of a question
as you might think.

00:13:35.780 --> 00:13:39.320
It's a rollerblade bike ride, snowmobile,
speedboat away from Los Angeles.

00:13:39.320 --> 00:13:41.750
Or, you know, a three hour
flight from L.A.X.

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:42.959
Even though the movie gives us all

00:13:42.959 --> 00:13:45.779
these convoluted directions
that seem so lol random.

00:13:45.779 --> 00:13:46.779
But they really laid out

00:13:46.779 --> 00:13:49.560
for us was a series of breadcrumbs,
giving us all the information we needed

00:13:49.560 --> 00:13:54.279
to track Barbie back to the source,
the literal source; her factory in Mexico.

00:13:54.279 --> 00:13:55.889
Sadly,
when you look at pictures of the place,

00:13:55.889 --> 00:13:57.830
though, it's not coated in neon pink.

00:13:57.830 --> 00:13:59.730
Maybe one day we can at least dream.

00:13:59.730 --> 00:14:00.730
But hey!

